{"schema_version": 1, "unit_id": "tag:0357:statement", "parent_tag": "033H", "chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "lemma", "risk_level": "R3", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme such that any quasi-compact open has a finite number\nof irreducible components. The following are equivalent:\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> <MATH_0002> is normal, and\n<STRUCT_0003> <MATH_0003> is a disjoint union of normal integral schemes.\n<STRUCT_0004>\n", "source_status": "CURRENT", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "MATH_0002": "$X$", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "MATH_0003": "$X$", "STRUCT_0004": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-normal-locally-finite-nr-irreducibles}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "source_text_hash": "sha256:bc8130312cfac569098ce7cdb885092532c7f17af6d234e027d96efdc8b27222", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:d00f05e98828df454be60a0bb46a680cdff1000449ee43cabf52aa2f5a29a87d", "source_math_hash": "sha256:b3055ea2944ed5fcda6131396aa9e9e6d3ca5169ca39bc6c9f17b2efc3c1e8ce"}
{"schema_version": 1, "unit_id": "tag:0357:proof", "parent_tag": "033H", "chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "proof", "risk_level": "R3", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_text": "It is immediate from the definitions that (2) implies (1).\nLet <MATH_0001> be a normal scheme such that every quasi-compact open\nhas a finite number of irreducible components.\nIf <MATH_0002> is affine then <MATH_0003> satisfies (2) by\nAlgebra, Lemma <REF_0001>.\nFor a general <MATH_0004>, let <MATH_0005> be\nan affine open covering. Note that also each <MATH_0006> has\nbut a finite number of irreducible components, and the lemma holds\nfor each <MATH_0007>. Let <MATH_0008> be an irreducible component.\nBy the affine case each intersection <MATH_0009> is open in <MATH_0010>\nand an integral normal scheme.\nHence <MATH_0011> is open, and an integral normal scheme.\nThis proves that <MATH_0012> is the disjoint union of its irreducible components,\nwhich are integral normal schemes.\n", "source_status": "CURRENT", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X$", "MATH_0002": "$X$", "MATH_0003": "$X$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{algebra-lemma-characterize-reduced-ring-normal}", "MATH_0004": "$X$", "MATH_0005": "$X = \\bigcup X_i$", "MATH_0006": "$X_i$", "MATH_0007": "$X_i$", "MATH_0008": "$T \\subset X$", "MATH_0009": "$T \\cap X_i$", "MATH_0010": "$X_i$", "MATH_0011": "$T \\subset X$", "MATH_0012": "$X$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "source_text_hash": "sha256:6aa90fe79c2c73fbecb9646a33f713235fab0b783e13de43179e47d0c0d6efd5", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:3cb91513f0ca0fc2a0df30507c3939e830ebe80a856102fb08fa6120e3d9adc4", "source_math_hash": "sha256:b21644c495a6c275f039a1e787b11ee3e79ce293c86c7ed84eb4b70a91c58108"}
